# App version vs service worker cache

These are **unrelated** version tracks. Do not bump them together by default.

## App release version (e.g. v2.2)

User-visible release label and asset cache-busting for normal HTTP loads.

Update together when shipping a labeled release:

- `app.js` — `VERSION` constant
- `hated-game/game.js` — `VERSION` constant
- `index.html` / `hated-game/index.html` — footer build label
- `?v=` query strings on stylesheets (e.g. `styles.css?v=…`, `guygames-ui.css?v=…`)
- `sw.js` **only** the precached URL strings that include `?v=` (must match HTML), **not** `CACHE_NAME`

## Service worker `CACHE_NAME`

Controls when the browser **drops the old offline precache bucket** and installs a fresh one (`sw.js` / `hated-game/sw.js`).

- **Independent** naming (e.g. `solitaire-picker-v2`, `hated-game-v2`) — not tied to app `v2.2`.
- **Bump only** when you intentionally need a hard SW cache reset (wrong/stale precached shell, changed precache strategy or `ASSETS` list in a way that leaves clients stuck).
- **Do not bump** for routine app changes (auth, UI, lib code, footer version bumps) — picker SW is network-first for `.js`/`.html`/`.css`, and `lib/*` is loaded via dynamic `import()`, so online users pick up changes on the next visit without renaming `CACHE_NAME`.

## Quick check

| Change | Bump app `VERSION` / `?v=` | Bump `CACHE_NAME` |
|--------|---------------------------|-------------------|
| Auth, leaderboard, account UI in `lib/` | Optional (if releasing) | No |
| Footer / display version | Yes | No |
| Fix broken offline precache | Maybe | Yes |
